' 17. Challenge an island challenger (Kana Wilds)
' Use case: Challenge an island challenger (Play Kana Wilds) · Actor: Learner
'
' Design patterns:
'   - Strategy: each challenger's signature defence is a defence style picked from a map
'     (nihon-web/src/lib/kanaWilds/defenceStyles.ts): Chun look-alikes, Tama shout, Pon stroke reveal, Sensei word
'     attacks, Zen recall (type the reading), Kurama brush
'   - Facade: rewardActivity() for the first win's XP (services/gamification.service.ts)
'   - Observer: achievement / level-up notifications published to every open tab
'   - Repository
' The challenge is played in the browser like a battle (readings graded by POST /api/quiz/answer, see diagram 16);
' the server saves the win once and pays XP the first time. Nothing is locked behind a win except the rewards below.
' Lifelines use BCE stereotypes: «boundary» screens, «control» use-case logic, «entity» stored data; the database
' keeps its own symbol.
@startuml 17 Challenge an island challenger
title 17. Challenge an island challenger (Kana Wilds)
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Learner
boundary "Web app\n(island)" as Web
control "Challenge rules\n(team + defence style)" as Rules
control "Kana Wilds controller\n+ service" as Wilds
control "Gamification\nservice" as Gam
entity "Repository" as Repo
database "Database" as DB
control "Notification\n(realtime)" as Notif

note over Web, Wilds : «Chain of responsibility»: headers → CORS → authenticate → controller\n«Decorator»: action() wraps every controller (error handling)

Learner -> Web : Open an island
Web -> Wilds : GET /api/kana-wilds/collection
Wilds -> Repo : collection, answers per kana, challenger wins
Repo -> DB : SELECT
Wilds --> Web : collection + beatenChallengers
Web -> Web : show the island; challenger marked "!" until beaten

Learner -> Web : Walk up to the challenger, press E (or tap Fight)
Web -> Rules : teamFor(challenger, collection)
note right of Rules : fixed team (Chun あこお …)\nor chosen from the learner's kana:\nZen the 3 weakest, Kurama 3 mixed
Rules --> Web : team + defence style
Web -> Web : show the challenger's lines and their team

loop each kana of the team, HP carried over
  Learner -> Web : Play words, defend their attacks
  Web -> Rules : pickAttack(style, enemy, words)
  note right of Rules : «Strategy»\nthe challenger's\nsignature defence
  Rules --> Web : attack
  note over Learner, Web : Same turns as diagram 16, without catching:\neach reading graded by POST /api/quiz/answer
end

alt won
  Web -> Wilds : POST /api/kana-wilds/challengers/:id/wins
  Wilds -> Wilds : known challenger? (404) starter chosen? (409)
  Wilds -> Repo : addChallengerWin()
  Repo -> DB : INSERT … ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
  opt first win against this challenger
    Wilds -> Gam : rewardActivity("game", "kana-wilds-challenger:<id>")
    note right of Gam : «Facade»
    Gam -> Repo : award XP, check achievements
    opt new achievement / level up
      Gam -> Notif : notify
      Notif -> DB : save notification
      Notif -> Web : publish → bell updates (all open tabs)
      note right of Notif : «Observer»
    end
    Gam --> Wilds : reward
  end
  Wilds --> Web : collection + isNew + reward
  Web -> Web : show the win, "+XP" and the reward
  note right of Web : Chun, Tama: new rows in a path's grass\nPon: Sharp Eyes (stroke count shown)\nSensei: voiced evolution (か → が)\nZen: small-kana evolution (き → きゃ)\nKurama: kept for the katakana wilds
  alt saving failed
    Web -> Web : show "Could not save your win" + Try again
  end
else lost or gave up
  Web -> Web : show the team, a tip and the kana mixed up ("You read ね as れ twice")
  opt try again
    Learner -> Web : Rematch
    note over Learner, Web : the loop starts again at once; a loss costs nothing
  end
end
@enduml
